<p>When 22-year-old student Christian LeBlanc fed a basket of bananas to a group of elephants on the Thai island of Koh Phangan in 2015, one of them seized his GoPro camera by its mount, and when the self-timer triggered the shutter he got <a href="https://imgur.com/gallery/elephant-selfie-nz2gf">&#8220;the worlds first ever Elfie.&#8221;</a></p>
<p>&#8220;Elephants are incredibly intelligent and it definitely makes you wonder if it was a conscious action,&#8221; he wrote. So who gets the credit? For now, <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Elephantselfie_with_Christian_LeBlanc.jpg">in the judgment of Wikimedia</a>, &#8220;This file is in the public domain because, as the work of a non-human animal, it has no human author in whom copyright is vested.&#8221;</p>
